# SR10: the four-card platform replay of the NEW production image: the node agent serving sequence in a copy of its container running the THIN LAYER
# (@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@: built by the operator on tp4-serve-10 AFTER S0 passes and pre-pulled into the rig daemon, by manifest-list digest). The replay sets no profile: it
# boots c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full BY THE IMAGE DEFAULT. READ the vLLM subprocess log from the container (never docker logs): '[QWEN-C2] profile c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full: vLLM argv', the P150x4 mesh, the
# extent block, the request-warm line BEFORE the block capture, admission passed with no UNQUALIFIED, Lever N and prefix installed, the prefill warm checks;
# the :tt alias advertised before and after the restart. Pass: 'PLATFORM_REPLAY passed=True' plus the thinking-budget smoke (C2_REPLAY_BUDGET_SMOKE=1, up to
# 90 min, fails the job if it ran and failed). The replay turns the session cap OFF, so the cap is read live after placement (ORDER, post-GO). The restart
# step is the first reopening of the mesh after an unclean exit: a wedge FAILS the replay. Real time ~60.
# TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the ship/262k-full pack (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over that file on a throwaway
# commit of ship/262k-full (with its evidence files committed) and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Names no rig, card, host or registry. ORDER.txt has
# the order, stop rules, real minutes, NEEDS and the GO rule. C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10 is the ONE shipping image X0B builds: every job serves it.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset replay
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-serve-10
C2_PLATFORM_IMAGE=@THIN_LAYER_IMAGE@
C2_REPLAY_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-full
C2_REPLAY_BUDGET_SMOKE=1
